{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794252447809,"sessionID":"ses_e3e3fc201ffewRTrqlUQgnln3y","part":{"id":"prt_1c1c7a01b001Z72p5twjk8ca8k","messageID":"msg_1c1c778ac001m6KLu4i2i3yPnZ","sessionID":"ses_e3e3fc201ffewRTrqlUQgnln3y","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794252447809,"sessionID":"ses_e3e3fc201ffewRTrqlUQgnln3y","part":{"id":"prt_1c1c7a01d001NwGhgIXpVQYNZL","messageID":"msg_1c1c778ac001m6KLu4i2i3yPnZ","sessionID":"ses_e3e3fc201ffewRTrqlUQgnln3y","type":"text","text":"The image gallery is built: the Flask API and the React frontend are both in place. Docker isn't installed here, so I couldn't build or run the image from the `Dockerfile`. Instead I ran the backend under gunicorn locally with the built frontend:\n- **Endpoints and errors:** every endpoint in the spec answered correctly, and the error cases returned the expected status codes.\n- **Files:** stored bytes came back identical with the right content type.\n- **Restart:** data was still there after restarting the server.\n- **Frontend:** it passes the type check and `npm run build`.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`):\n- SQLite database and image files are stored under `./data`.\n- Login tokens are random strings, stored hashed, and expire after 30 days.\n- The format is detected from the file's first bytes, so a PNG named `pic.jpg` is stored as `image/png`. Anything that isn't PNG or JPEG gets a 400 with a message.\n- Uploads with the same filename are kept as separate images.\n- Status codes for the main error cases:\n\n| Case | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Username already taken | 409 |\n| Missing or invalid token | 401 |\n| Deleting someone else's image | 403 |\n| Image not found | 404 |\n\n**Things I added or decided that you didn't specify:**\n- **Extra endpoints:** `GET /api/auth/me` (used to restore a session on page load) and `POST /api/auth/logout`.\n- **Size limits:** images can be at most 10 MB, and `page_size` is capped at 100.\n- **Defaults:** `page_size` defaults to 20, and the frontend shows 12 images per page.\n- **Username matching:** usernames ignore case, so \"Alice\" and \"alice\" are the same account.\n- **Dockerfile:** I changed the pip step to install directly from `requirements.lock` with `--require-hashes`. The original command failed on the pip version in my local venv (25.1) because the lock file contains hashes. I haven't checked which pip the `python:3.13-slim` image ships, but the new form works either way.\n- **Ignore files:** `data` is now excluded from the Docker build context, and I added a `.gitignore`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src`): Tailwind v4 (the only CSS file is its `index.css` entry) and TypeScript, with a new `npm run typecheck` script. It covers:\n- sign-in and registration tabs, with the username and a sign-out button in the header;\n- a responsive thumbnail grid with title or filename, uploader and date, plus paging and an empty state;\n- a full-size viewer showing filename, title and size;\n- an upload form limited to PNG and JPEG, with a preview and the API's error messages;\n- a delete button with a confirmation dialog on your own images.","time":{"start":1794252447773,"end":1794252447776}}}
